Conjugate gradients: one Polak-Ribiere+ beta, descent fallback, count every step

ConjugateGradientsTakeNSteps mixed beta atom by atom -- each atom's |g|^2
over the squared length of its own previous *direction* -- which builds
neither conjugate directions nor, necessarily, downhill ones. On taxol the
method was still descending after 5000 steps under UFF, MMFF94 and GAFF.

Compute beta once over all coordinates (Polak-Ribiere+, clipped at 0, so
the method restarts itself whenever the gradient turns against the
previous one), and fall back to steepest descent when the resulting
direction is not a descent direction. The previous direction and force
live in _grad1, now 2 * _ncoords long.

ConjugateGradientsInitialize took a line-search step of its own that no
step counter saw: ConjugateGradients(n) ran n + 1 line searches, and a
caller driving Initialize/TakeNSteps could not count the first. Initialize
now only sets up; the first TakeNSteps step is the steepest-descent one.

